refs/kitaev-2405.02434/approximate_algebras.tex:1194-1196 VERBATIM: "\begin{Proposition}\label{prop_delta_hominc}
Let $v\colon \calA'\to\calA''$ be a non-unital $\delta$-homomorphism of $\eps$-$C^*$ algebras. Then in general, $\|v\|\le 1+O(\delta+\eps)$. If $\|v(X)\|\ge\eta\|X\|$ for some $\eta>2\delta$ and all $X$, then $\|v(X)\|\ge a\|X\|$ for $a=1-O(\delta+\eps)$ and all $X$. Furthermore, if $\|v(I_{\calA'})-I_{\calA''}\|$ is less than a certain positive constant, then $\|v(I_{\calA'})-I_{\calA''}\|\le O(\delta+\eps)$.
\end{Proposition}" [Kitaev arXiv:2405.02434 Proposition prop_delta_hominc, statement lines 1194-1196; proof retained in-source at :1198-1222 (NOT imported); smallness/implicit-quantification convention at :1192 (constants eps_max, delta_max exist such that for all eps<=eps_max, delta<=delta_max); data-independence of big-O at :458 (each big-O is a concrete function, not depending on any additional data). Imports exactly the printed Proposition statement: non-unital delta-homomorphism norm bound ||v||<=1+O(delta+eps); lower-bound upgrade eta>2delta => a=1-O(delta+eps); near-unitality upgrade ||v(I')-I''||<=O(delta+eps).]
